7	 A browser multiplayer pirate treasure race. The game is specified in [`docs/spec.md`](docs/spec.md) (the text of `docs/spec.docx`); [`docs/architecture.md`](docs/architecture.md) maps this repository onto it.
8	 
9	-Browsers create or join a private match by a six-character code and sail placeholder ships around the slice sea: four small islands with docks, shoals, and eight outer-sea spawn slots. Up (or W) sails ahead, down (S) brakes and then reverses, left and right (A, D) turn, and E docks a slow ship beside a dock. The authoritative server decides every position and sends each browser only the ships within its sight radius; the minimap's fog clears where the player has sailed.
10	+Browsers create or join a private match by a six-character code and sail placeholder ships around the slice sea: a compact map with four small islands with docks, reefs and shoal walls that funnel every route between islands through one central crossing, and eight outer-sea spawn slots. Up (or W) sails ahead, down (S) brakes and then reverses, left and right (A, D) turn, and E docks a slow ship beside a dock. The authoritative server decides every position and sends each browser only the ships within its sight radius; the minimap's fog clears where the player has sailed.
11	 
12	 The combat spike (§18 stage 1) runs beside it: "Create duel" makes a 1v1 duel whose code the second browser enters under "Join duel", and "Practice" fights a server-side dummy (idle or guarding). After a three-second countdown both browsers predict the fight with the shared duel simulation and roll back to the server's inputs (`docs/duel.md`). Keys (§8): WASD or the arrows move (hold back to guard), J light, K heavy, U and I specials, Shift dash, J and K together throw. The HUD shows both health bars, stamina, the round clock, the connection line (round trip, input delay, corrections) and the result; "Show hitboxes" draws hurtboxes and active hitboxes.
