 A browser multiplayer pirate treasure race. The game is specified in [`docs/spec.md`](docs/spec.md) (the text of `docs/spec.docx`); [`docs/architecture.md`](docs/architecture.md) maps this repository onto it.

-Browsers create or join a private match by a six-character code and sail placeholder ships around the slice sea: four small islands with docks, shoals, and eight outer-sea spawn slots. Up (or W) sails ahead, down (S) brakes and then reverses, left and right (A, D) turn, and E docks a slow ship beside a dock. The authoritative server decides every position and sends each browser only the ships within its sight radius; the minimap's fog clears where the player has sailed.
+Browsers create or join a private match by a six-character code and sail placeholder ships around the slice sea: a compact map with four small islands with docks, reefs and shoal walls that funnel every route between islands through one central crossing, and eight outer-sea spawn slots. Up (or W) sails ahead, down (S) brakes and then reverses, left and right (A, D) turn, and E docks a slow ship beside a dock. The authoritative server decides every position and sends each browser only the ships within its sight radius; the minimap's fog clears where the player has sailed.

 The combat spike (§18 stage 1) runs beside it: "Create duel" makes a 1v1 duel whose code the second browser enters under "Join duel", and "Practice" fights a server-side dummy (idle or guarding). After a three-second countdown both browsers predict the fight with the shared duel simulation and roll back to the server's inputs (`docs/duel.md`). Keys (§8): WASD or the arrows move (hold back to guard), J light, K heavy, U and I specials, Shift dash, J and K together throw. The HUD shows both health bars, stamina, the round clock, the connection line (round trip, input delay, corrections) and the result; "Show hitboxes" draws hurtboxes and active hitboxes.

@@ -31,7 +31,7 @@ Set `VITE_SERVER_URL` when the web client should reach a server other than port

 **Simulated latency for duel playtests (development only).** With `npm run dev`, add `?rtt=80&jitter=20` to the page's address (for example `http://localhost:5393/?rtt=80&jitter=20`) before creating or joining a duel: that browser's duel socket is then delayed by half the round trip each way, plus a uniform ±jitter/2, in order, round-trip probes included, so the HUD's round trip and the chosen input delay reflect it. Give both browsers the setting to test §19's 30, 80 or 150 ms. It is read only when `import.meta.env.DEV` is true and is absent from the production build (`npm run build` checks). Loss is simulated only by the test harness (`ImpairmentProxy` in `packages/test-tools`).

-Edit the map in [Tiled](https://www.mapeditor.org/) within the subset documented in `packages/content/src/tiledMap.ts`, then run `npm run map:build`.
+The map is generated from an ASCII sketch of one quarter, `assets/source/maps/sketch.ts`: edit it, run `node assets/source/maps/sketch.ts`, then `npm run map:build` (details in `assets/source/maps/README.md`). The `.tmj` stays within the Tiled subset documented in `packages/content/src/tiledMap.ts`, so [Tiled](https://www.mapeditor.org/) opens it.

